    "result_text": "All tests green (3/3, BUILD SUCCESS). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional `postcode` field with region-aware validation while keeping structural impact low \u2014 **no existing method was modified**, so the high-complexity `addOwner` and the rest of the large controller/entity classes were left untouched.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` property to `OwnerFields` with `pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'` (format validation \u2192 400 for malformed like `\"12\"`), and a class-level `x-class-extra-annotation` wiring the DTO to the new cross-field constraint. This mirrors the repo's existing `x-field-extra-annotation` usage for `PetAgeValidation`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column field plus two trivial accessors (needed for persistence; MapStruct maps them by name automatically, so no mapper change).\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`data.sql`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column (ddl-auto is `none` for the test profile) and updated the positional seed inserts.\n\n4. **New `PostcodeValidation` + `PostcodeValidator`** (mirroring the existing `PetAgeValidation`/`PetAgeValidator` pattern) \u2014 a small, self-contained cross-field validator that rejects an out-of-range postcode for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), passes any 4-digit postcode for unknown-region cities, and treats absent/non-4-digit values as valid (absence is optional; format is enforced by the field pattern).\n\nBecause Bean Validation runs on the `@Valid @RequestBody`, both the malformed and out-of-range cases surface as `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** through the existing advice, with zero changes to any existing function. The new logic lives entirely in fresh classes with no surrounding complexity.",
